			<div id="congrats">
				<h2>Congratulations to girls who are helping in ways that are big and small</h2>
				<p>Just like Grand-Prize Winners Bailey, Madison, and Ellen, girls across the country are contributing to their families and communities in unique ways, every day. American Girl thanks you for your compassion, creativity, and helpfulness. You&#8217;re truly making a difference&#8212;just like the inspiration for the contest, our 2007 Girl of the Year character, <a href="agd://www.americangirl.com/goty/2007Nicki/index.html">Nicki Fleming</a>. </p>
				<p>For more inspiring stories, meet the Honorable Mention Award Winners and Finalists, girls whose brightest moments will bring a smile to your face.</p>
			</div>
			<div id="list">
				<h3>Here are 5 easy ways to start helping others, inspired by Real Girl of the Year contest entries:</h3>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Be caring</strong> - Instead of a birthday gift, ask for donations to a favorite charity</li>
					<li><strong>Be creative</strong> - Send care packages to soldiers serving overseas</li>
					<li><strong>Be compassionate</strong> - Spend time talking with an elderly neighbor</li>
					<li><strong>Be responsible</strong> - Write to local officials about an environmental issue</li>
					<li><strong>Be helpful</strong> - Invite the new kid at school to join your lunch table</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
